<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Swede Ridge Shelter Loop</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:272-3: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.989467" lon="-121.568160"><ele>1769.6</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead th:swampy-lakes-sno-park (OSM relation 11960476); confidence: high; pdf_page: 273; book_elev_ft: 5700; quote: map 62: SWAMPY LAKES SNO-PARK 5700'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.003490" lon="-121.584270"><ele>1810.9</ele><name>West end of the Swampy Lakes flats (Swampy Tie junction)</name><desc>source: OSM: Swampy Lakes Trail #23 (way 279479053) meets Swampy Tie Trail #23.1 (way 878847315); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 274; quote: Ski first to the Swampy Lakes Shelter</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.004301" lon="-121.583655"><ele>1807.6</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Shelter</name><desc>source: OSM node 5716237824 Swampy Shelter; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 274; book_elev_ft: 5880; quote: The shelter sits on the north side of the wide meadow and 100 yards into the trees.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.003490" lon="-121.584270"><ele>1810.9</ele><name>West end of the flats (back from the shelter)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 274; quote: From the shelter return to the meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.008719" lon="-121.585411"><ele>1794.6</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Trail north of the shelter</name><desc>source: OSM node 2898555286: Swampy Lakes Trail #23 meets Swampy Loop Trail #23.2 on the north side of the flats; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 273; quote: map 62: from the shelter the trail runs east along the north side (0.5) to the North Leg</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.008234" lon="-121.580584"><ele>1788.0</ele><name>Start of the North Leg (Swede Ridge Trail #52)</name><desc>source: OSM node 8175960219, west end of Swede Ridge Trail #52 (way 286537814) on the Swampy Loop piste; confidence: high; pdf_page: 274; quote: then ski east to Swede Ridge Loop Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.015182" lon="-121.547722"><ele>1735.5</ele><name>Swede Ridge Shelter clearing (trail end)</name><desc>source: OSM node 2898618383, east end of trail #52 and top of Forest Road 4615-100; shelter node 2898613044 is 60 m north-west; confidence: high; pdf_page: 274; quote: You eventually arrive at a clearcut, and the shelter is at its northeast corner in the trees.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.015437" lon="-121.548262"><ele>1734.0</ele><name>Swede Ridge Shelter</name><desc>source: OSM node 2898613044 Swede Ridge Shelter; confidence: high; pdf_page: 274; quote: the shelter is at its northeast corner in the trees</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.015182" lon="-121.547722"><ele>1735.5</ele><name>Swede Ridge Shelter clearing (back)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: high; pdf_page: 274; quote: To return, descend the clearcut near the shelter</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.007657" lon="-121.560140"><ele>1756.6</ele><name>Road meets the South Leg (Loop Tie junction)</name><desc>source: OSM node 2898617822: Forest Road 4615-100 / 4615-140 (piste Swede Ridge Loop) meet Swede Ridge Loop Trail #53; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 274; quote: skiing to its far end where you meet a road. Follow the road briefly to where the Loop Tie Trail joins</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.996338" lon="-121.579325"><ele>1810.3</ele><name>South Leg meets Swampy Lakes Trail</name><desc>source: OSM node 2898561958: Swede Ridge Loop Trail #53 (way 878847231) joins Swampy Lakes Trail #23; confidence: high; pdf_page: 275; quote: follow the Swede Ridge Loop's south leg as it crosses a divide and meets the Swampy Lakes Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.989467" lon="-121.568160"><ele>1769.6</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high; pdf_page: 275; book_elev_ft: 5700; quote: which goes south to the sno-park on a wide snow-covered road</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Swede Ridge Shelter Loop</name><desc>1. Swampy Lakes Sno-Park -&gt; West end of the Swampy Lakes flats (Swampy Tie junction): osm (high), 1.52 mi | 2. West end of the Swampy Lakes flats (Swampy Tie junction) -&gt; Swampy Lakes Shelter: straight (medium), 0.06 mi | 3. Swampy Lakes Shelter -&gt; West end of the flats (back from the shelter): straight (medium), 0.06 mi | 4. West end of the flats (back from the shelter) -&gt; Swampy Lakes Trail north of the shelter: osm (medium), 0.59 mi | 5. Swampy Lakes Trail north of the shelter -&gt; Start of the North Leg (Swede Ridge Trail #52): osm (medium), 0.25 mi | 6. Start of the North Leg (Swede Ridge Trail #52) -&gt; Swede Ridge Shelter clearing (trail end): osm (high), 1.92 mi | 7. Swede Ridge Shelter clearing (trail end) -&gt; Swede Ridge Shelter: straight (high), 0.03 mi | 8. Swede Ridge Shelter -&gt; Swede Ridge Shelter clearing (back): straight (high), 0.03 mi | 9. Swede Ridge Shelter clearing (back) -&gt; Road meets the South Leg (Loop Tie junction): osm (medium), 0.98 mi | 10. Road meets the South Leg (Loop Tie junction) -&gt; South Leg meets Swampy Lakes Trail: osm (high), 1.88 mi | 11. South Leg meets Swampy Lakes Trail -&gt; Swampy Lakes Sno-Park (finish): osm (medium), 0.93 mi</desc>
